Z||000003||Oreif||02-27-2000||10:20 PM||||I thought hugger orange was a GTO Judge color? I had a 1976 Astre  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> (OK OK quit laughing it was my first car in 1979 they didn't make Fiero's ...YET) painted that way with white stripes. Color is very nice. Never saw it on a Fiero but I imagine it would look great! I say GO FOR IT!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Astre.jpg">   <P>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 02-27-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 02-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||02-27-2000||11:30 PM||||In the latest issue of High Performance Pontiac there is a pic of an orange GT dragracing at some Pontiac meet. I thought it looked petty cool. I have seen some 2K model Z28's in orange- a little different from the old GM Hugger Orange but pretty cool. And just to defuse any more "eewww"-like comments, it's your car, you drive it, you can paint it any color you like. Just remember that green is bad luck.||||reg||1
